            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>Some archetypes are driven to provide structure to the world, while others want to encourage a connection with others in their unique way and then there are the archetypes who yearn for paradise.</p>
                <p>But Hero’s? Well, they are the archetype’s who want to leave a mark on the world by being proactive - they want to shake things up and change things.</p>
                <p>Definitely, the way that a Hero Archetype will shake things up is through attaining mastery. Though sometimes, the Hero’s actions will seem to be far away from the discipline that you might expect to arise out of mastery!</p>
                <p>A Hero can be found sorting out problems, saving people and putting out fires.  That’s how they change the world. You will also see them promoting acts of courage and bravery and even creating businesses that will make the world a better place.</p> 
                <p>You will also find them promoting acts of courage and bravery and even creating businesses that will make the world a better place. </p> 
                <p>Hero’s are (but are not limited to) the entrepreneurs, the high level CEO’s, Doctors, tradesmen, troubleshooters, consultants and athletes of our world.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step1-back hover prev f-left">1. Introduction</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step3 hover f-right">3. Sense of Significance</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">                
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.If we don&rsquo;t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our wellbeing begins to deplete.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Hero Archetype, they contribute by demonstrating their courage and bravery at every turn.The Hero&rsquo;s action toward their goals or ideals will always come before their fears or limitations can stop them.</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s with this strong sense of courage and the desire to make their mark on the world that the Hero will fight whatever cause they are aligned with to the end. They will ensure that they attain their goals - which will usually be focused on something that the Hero feels is important for the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>A Hero can become overly heroic in the home if they don&rsquo;t have a particular problem or project to focus on.Actions such as working too hard to provide or jumping in and saving their children from problems that they should learn to deal with themselves will be common.If a Hero doesn&rsquo;t have something to capture their attention, then the people around them will become the focus of their attention.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>All people need to feel as though they contribute to the world around them, some in smaller ways than other sand all will struggle to find joy in life without contributing, but a Hero Archetype, in particular, will suffer greatly if they do not have something that they can do.And that something must challenge them and must also make a difference.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The problem is though that for a Hero they need to feel a sense of contribution like no other archetype.As we move through this report, we will discover how Hero Archetypes can bring problems to their door through this need to be the one who contributes significantly. We even discover how the Hero creates these problems and how they can manage this problem in the future - leaving them free to continue their life&rsquo;s work without being too excessive or unfulfilled with the projects they are focused on.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Pushing things too far, and a desperate need to validate themselves are some of the Hero&rsquo;s greatest challenges when it comes to establishing a sense of contribution and significance, and for many, it&rsquo;s also their biggest challenge in all aspects of their life too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>There&rsquo;s No Problem That A Hero Can&rsquo;t Help With &hellip; Or Is There?</strong></p>
                <p>A Hero Archetype is likely to be competitive, and can sometimes appear to be calculated or aggressive.This is usually because their desire to get the job done not just in the best way possible but to be the best at what they are working on is unlimited.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This doesn&rsquo;t always make a Hero Archetype popular with the crowds, at least not with the people such as work colleagues who have seen the Hero in action many times before - but who have not taken the time to get to know them properly.</p>
                <p>The problem is though that a Hero is limited to his or her human capabilities and there are some things that a Hero might be faced with that they can&rsquo;t handle.This situation is tough for a Hero Archetype, their (secretly fragile) sense of self relies on confirmation that they have some problem-solving prowess and when they can&rsquo;t solve a problem, it&rsquo;s a big deal for the Hero.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Perhaps Heroes do not believe in themselves and need to constantly prove it to themselves that they are proficient in all they do.This is for sure something that a Hero would benefit from exploring.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Although some Heroes may have already come to realize the reasons why they might have such a need to &lsquo;prove&rsquo; themselves, others have the opportunity to learn more about this aspect of themselves.They can do so by working with their shadow self so that they can reconcile this situation and give themselves the opportunity to build themselves up in a sustainable and life-changing way.If they accomplish this, then they reap the rewards of their contribution more than they could have ever imagined they were capable of.</p>
